  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 36. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 国々 — いろいろな国。\n2. 配り物 — 人に分けて渡す物。\n3. 首飾り — 首の周りにつける飾り。\n4. 組み分け — いくつかの組に分けること。\n5. 暗がり — 光が少なくて暗い所。\n6. 暮らし — 毎日を過ごすことや生活の様子。\n7. クリーナー — 汚れなどを落とすための道具や薬剤。\n8. 胡桃割り — クルミのかたい殻を割るための道具。\n9. 黒字 — 収入が支出を上回っていること。\n10. 黒塗り — 黒い色で塗ること。\n11. 企て — 何かをしようとして立てる計画。\n12. 毛穴 — 皮膚で毛が生えている小さな穴。\n13. 掲載 — 新聞や本やウェブなどに文章や写真を載せること。\n14. 決定 — どうするかをはっきり決めること。\n15. 血圧 — 流れる血液が血管の壁を押す圧力。\n16. 血液 — 体の中を流れて酸素や栄養などを運ぶ液体。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
